Feature: Unity Catalog Schema Design for purgo_playground

  Background:
    Given the sample sales data is loaded from "sample_sales_data.csv"
    And the source data contains fields: country_cd, product_id, qty_sold, sales_date

  # Happy Path Scenarios
  Scenario: Successful schema creation for purgo_playground
    Given I have the objectives and purpose for the schema
    And I understand the expected data flow and integration
    And user roles along with the required access levels are defined
    And I know the necessary data processing and transformations
    And expected outputs or reports from the schema are outlined
    And I have the data update frequency and methods
    When I create the purgo_playground schema
    Then the schema should be compliant with all the outlined objectives
    And all user roles have appropriate access privileges
    And the schema integrates seamlessly with existing systems
    And data processing occurs as expected producing correct outputs

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven validation of schema fields
    Given I am validating the schema with the following data
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date  |
      | <country>  | <product>  | <qty>    | <date>      |
    When I check the field <field>
    Then the data must conform to the expected format
    
    Examples:
      | field       | country | product | qty | date       |
      | country_cd  | US      | P1001   | 50  | 2024-01-15 |
      | product_id  | CA      | P1003   | 25  | 2024-01-17 |
      | qty_sold    | UK      | P1002   | 35  | 2024-01-18 |
      | sales_date  | IN      | P1001   | 60  | 2024-01-20 |

  # Error Scenarios
  Scenario: Schema creation failure due to missing objectives
    Given the objectives for the purgo_playground schema are not defined
    When I attempt to create the schema
    Then the system should prevent creation
    And I should see an error message "Schema creation failed: Objectives undefined."

  Scenario: Access control violation
    Given the schema is created successfully
    And user roles and access levels are incorrectly defined
    When a user tries to access restricted data
    Then access should be denied
    And the error message "Access denied: insufficient privileges" should be displayed

  Scenario: Data processing error due to incorrect transformation rules
    Given I have defined incorrect data transformation rules
    When I execute the data processing on the schema
    Then the process should fail
    And an error message "Data processing error: Transformation rules error" should be shown

  # Technical Details
  Scenario: Validate data type and format
    Given the sample_sales_data.csv is available
    When I validate the data types
    Then country_cd should be a string of length 2
    And product_id should be a string prefixed with 'P'
    And qty_sold should be an integer
    And sales_date should be in the format YYYY-MM-DD

  Scenario: Scheduled data updates are applied
    Given the data update frequency is daily
    And the update method is batch processing at midnight
    When the update occurs
    Then the new data should be available in the schema the next morning
    And no data loss should occur

  # Examples for multiple test cases are included inline as per Scenario Outline.

